      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We describe a patient with dysphagia and chest pain, whose sole esophageal manometric abnormality was an elevated lower esophageal sphincter pressure. A radionuclide esophageal emptying test showed prolongation of emptying. After bougienage and medications failed to give relief, pneumatic dilatation gave excellent subjective and objective results."},
